@DaveNadig Not to be pedantic, but I think this just depends upon your definition of "accountable."

Reporters are not judge, jury, and executioner.

But what reporters uncover plays an important role in people being held accountable for their actions.

@DaveNadig Where did I say anything even close to that?  

Investigative journalism is extremely important.

Again, my point is only that they don't get to define what appropriate accountability is.
